ndia.indiatimes.com/photo/135931963.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/squandered-nations-best-opportunity-ex-ally-akhil-gogoi-accuses-congress-of-weakening-cjp-agitation/articleshow/135931963.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/squandered-nations-best-opportunity-ex-ally-akhil-gogoi-accuses-congress-of-weakening-cjp-agitation/articleshow/135931963.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-17T21:21:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135932128,imgsize-1536178.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Who ransacked Halebidu?' BJP hits back at Rahul Gandhi over Hoysaleshwara Temple post]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/who-ransacked-halebidu-bjp-hits-back-at-rahul-gandhi-over-hoysaleshwara-temple-post/articleshow/135929980.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135929980.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Bharatiya Janata Party responded sharply to Rahul Gandhi's remarks regarding the emotional well-being of BJP and RSS supporters. They pressed him to confront the historical invasions that caused the ruin of Halebidu, demanding recognition of the invaders' identities. Assam's Chief Minister, Himanta Biswa Sarma, joined the dialogue, challenging Gandhi's portrayal of mortals as divine figures during a book launch where Gandhi shared familial experiences.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/who-ransacked-halebidu-bjp-hits-back-at-rahul-gandhi-over-hoysaleshwara-temple-post/articleshow/135929980.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/who-ransacked-halebidu-bjp-hits-back-at-rahul-gandhi-over-hoysaleshwara-temple-post/articleshow/135929980.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-17T20:15:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aadrita Halder</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135930039,imgsize-30030.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Multiple NEET attempts, weightage to class 12 scores: States' suggestions to Nilekani panel]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/multiple-neet-attempts-weightage-to-class-12-scores-states-suggestions-to-nilekani-panel/articleshow/135929461.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135929461.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Multiple states are advocating for a system that enables students to attempt the NEET-UG exam more than once a year. Additional proposals suggest integrating Class 12 board exam results into the admissions framework. A high-powered task force, spearheaded by Nandan Nilekani, is currently evaluating feedback from various participants. The Centre has also extended the report submission deadline to January 2027, focusing on bolstering exam security and mitigating question paper leaks.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/multiple-neet-attempts-weightage-to-class-12-scores-states-suggestions-to-nilekani-panel/articleshow/135929461.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/multiple-neet-attempts-weightage-to-class-12-scores-states-suggestions-to-nilekani-panel/articleshow/135929461.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-17T20:07:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135929741,imgsize-62006.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Two Indian seafarers hurt, 1 missing after tanker targeted in Hormuz Strait]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/two-ind